From 0da488109a06a9d39d5e17458c089b040b87c2eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: overdoingism <overdoingism@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 22:03:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cuda: RDNA4 verify-step fusions: GLU -> Q8_1, GDN conv
 at 2..255 tokens, batched state-snapshot copies

Three speculative-verify fusions, each bit-identical, default-on on RDNA4 and with its own kill switch:

- GLU -> Q8_1 (GGML_CUDA_FUSE_GLU_Q8_1=0 off): when the next node (or the one after a reshape) is a verify-band
  mmvq matmul over an F32 GLU, the GLU launcher also writes that matmul's Q8_1 activation into the quantize
  cache, so the matmul skips its quantize_q8_1 launch. It reuses unary_gated_q8_1_op_kernel (the unary * mul
  -> Q8_1 fold), which now optionally also writes the F32 output. ggml_cuda_try_fuse records the GLU / matmul
  pair in two ggml_backend_cuda_context fields that every try_fuse call resets and the GLU launcher consumes.
  The decision goes through ggml_cuda_should_fuse_mul_mat_vec_q(mm, true), so it is RDNA4-only and follows
  GGML_CUDA_FUSE_Q8_1_VERIFY as well.
- GDN conv at 2..255 tokens (GGML_CUDA_FUSE_GDN_CONV_VERIFY=0 off): gdn_conv_check also accepts T >= 2 on RDNA4,
  so the verify step's CONCAT is no longer a generic non-contiguous copy per layer. Same kernels.
- Batched copy (GGML_CUDA_FUSE_CPY_BATCH=0 off; RDNA4, not with concurrent streams): consecutive f32 CPY nodes
  with the same source and destination layout (the per-position conv-state snapshots, with the VIEW nodes
  between them) go out as one launch, after checking that no copy's destination overlaps another copy's source
  or destination. GGML_CUDA_FUSE_CPY_BATCH_DEBUG=1 prints every run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
